<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Lorde comes for her yearly preventive visit, three weeks after her one-year survivorship visit. She is thirteen months from a right mastectomy for stage IA hormone receptor-positive breast cancer and has taken tamoxifen daily for a year. Her left mammogram four weeks ago was normal. She saw the genetic counselor two weeks ago, and the panel result is expected in about two weeks. Her hot flashes are mild and settled with the cooling measures she has used since the spring. Her periods come every 28 to 35 days and are lighter than before tamoxifen, with no bleeding between periods. She walks most days and is writing well. She completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 45</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Stage IA right breast cancer after mastectomy, on adjuvant tamoxifen</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Tamoxifen 20 mg daily</td></tr><tr><td>Gynecologic</td><td>Cycles every 28 to 35 days, lighter; no intermenstrual or postcoital bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; walking about 200 minutes a week</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Close family and a wide circle of friends and fellow writers; no financial strain; feels safe at home</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; a glass of wine a few times a month; walks most days; cooks most meals with vegetables and whole grains</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages her own medicines, money, travel, and household</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; wears a seat belt; no firearms in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; eye examination last year; no hearing concern</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night; hot flashes wake her about once a week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

