    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression screen negative; AUDIT-C 1. Cervical sample taken as part of the yearly gynecologic assessment advised while she takes tamoxifen. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Stage IA right breast cancer, on tamoxifen, no evidence of recurrence (C50.411)</content>. No symptoms or signs of recurrence; left mammogram BI-RADS 1 four weeks ago. Normal periods without abnormal bleeding on tamoxifen. [S]<list><item>Continue tamoxifen 20 mg daily.</item><item>Survivorship visit in January; genetic panel result reviewed when it returns.</item><item>Next left mammogram one year after the last.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Cardiovascular risk</content>. Total cholesterol 182, HDL 64, LDL 98, triglycerides 100 mg/dL; blood pressure 118/74; non-smoker; HbA1c 5.4%. Low 10-year risk; no statin indicated. [S]<list><item>Continue current activity and diet.</item><item>Recheck lipids in five years, or sooner if risk changes.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 2026-2027</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; she will get it at her pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended for adults 19 to 59; series to start at the January visit if the screening test shows no immunity</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap seven and a half years ago; next due in about two and a half years</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster and pneumococcal vaccines</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended from age 50; tamoxifen is not immunosuppressive</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Replaced by surveillance: yearly diagnostic mammogram of the left breast, last done four weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Cytology with HPV co-testing; last screening more than five years ago; result pending</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Recommended from 45; after discussing the options she chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test; kit given</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening; no prior result on record; drawn today, results pending</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>LDL 98 mg/dL; low 10-year risk; no statin</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>HbA1c 5.4% (BMI 25.3)</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/74 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; feels safe at home</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density testing</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Premenopausal on tamoxifen alone; calcium and vitamin D from diet and weight-bearing exercise advised</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity and diet counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walking about 200 minutes a week; add strength exercise twice a week</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Cervical screening, hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV results by portal message. Fecal immunochemical test returned by mail. Survivorship visit in January with the genetic panel result. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

